{"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:dependence-free-batch-d-reviewer-fable-22","reviews":[{"case_id":"case:465d8368b0cdc3b167fd","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope","bounded_statement":null,"root_cause":null,"issue_class":null,"evidence_atoms":[{"description":"The input data contain exactly 24 data rows and 24 distinct site_id values (DS01 through DS24), each appearing on exactly one row, so no independent unit enters the cross-tabulation more than once. Verified by listing all site codes from line 2 through line 25 of the CSV.","observed_value":{"data_rows":24,"unique_site_ids":24,"duplicated_site_ids":0},"source_spans":[{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":1,"end_line":2,"quoted_text":"site_id,restoration_method,slack_area_m2,years_since_works,helleborine_present\nDS01,inversion,1840,6,yes"},{"path":"data/input.csv","start_line":25,"end_line":25,"quoted_text":"DS24,stripping,1180,5,no"}]},{"description":"The workflow code explicitly enforces one row per independent unit: it raises a hard error if any site_id appears on more than one row before any statistics are computed, so a duplicated unit could not silently reach the Fisher test.","observed_value":"ValueError raised on duplicated site_id","source_spans":[{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":28,"end_line":30,"quoted_text":"codes = [slack[\"site_id\"] for slack in slacks]\n    if len(codes) != len(set(codes)):\n        raise ValueError(\"site_id must appear on exactly one row\")"}]},{"description":"The data description states each slack was surveyed and entered exactly once, ruling out repeated-measures structure hidden behind single rows, and confirms site_id values are unique.","observed_value":"one survey per slack; site_id unique per row","source_spans":[{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":14,"end_line":16,"quoted_text":"The slacks are separated by dune ridges, were restored under separate\ncontracts, and none of them was surveyed or entered twice, so each site yields a\nsingle yes/no outcome and nothing more."},{"path":"data-description.md","start_line":20,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"- `site_id` - unique code for the slack, DS01 to DS24; appears on one row only."}]},{"description":"Independent recomputation of the 2x2 table from the raw CSV gives inversion 9 present / 3 absent and stripping 3 present / 9 absent, odds ratio 9.00, and two-sided Fisher exact p = 2*(52901/2704156) = 0.0391, exactly matching the report; the reported result is therefore reproduced from unduplicated per-site rows.","observed_value":{"table":[[9,3],[3,9]],"odds_ratio":9,"two_sided_p":0.0391},"source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":19,"end_line":20,"quoted_text":"| Deep topsoil inversion | 9 | 3 | 12 | 75.0% |\n| Turf stripping | 3 | 9 | 12 | 25.0% |"},{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":26,"end_line":26,"quoted_text":"- Fisher's exact test, two-sided: p = 0.0391"}]}],"counterevidence_atoms":[{"description":"The procedure used is of the row-independent type that this issue class targets: Fisher's exact test applied to rows treated as independent Bernoulli outcomes. This makes the analysis susceptible in principle if a unit were duplicated, but inspection of the data and code shows no duplication occurred, so this precondition alone does not demonstrate the issue.","observed_value":"row-independent procedure present; no duplicated unit found","source_spans":[{"path":"results/report.md","start_line":5,"end_line":7,"quoted_text":"Each row of `data/input.csv` is one restored dune slack, walked once during the\n2025 flowering season. No slack contributes more than one row, so the 24 rows\nare 24 independent units and a row-independent test is appropriate."},{"path":"workflow/analysis.py","start_line":12,"end_line":12,"quoted_text":"from scipy.stats import fisher_exact"}]}],"falsification_attempt":"I attempted to demonstrate the issue by (1) checking every site_id in data/input.csv for repeats: DS01-DS24 each appear exactly once across the 24 data rows; (2) looking for near-duplicate covariate rows (same method/area/age) that could indicate a re-entered site under a different code: all area values are distinct; (3) tracing the code path for any aggregation, merge, resampling, or loop that could feed a row into the 2x2 table more than once: cross_tabulate increments exactly one cell per row and read_slacks raises on duplicated codes; (4) recomputing the table, odds ratio (9.00), and two-sided Fisher p-value (0.0391) from the raw CSV, which matched the report exactly, confirming the reported result derives from one entry per independent unit. All attempts to exhibit a repeated independent-unit entry failed.","cross_case_evidence_used":false,"unresolved_material_questions":[],"self_reported_confidence":"high"}]}